(1 Introduction Recurrent networks process a sequence one position at a time,) Tj
T*
(carrying a hidden state forward. This sequential structure is the source of) Tj
T*
(both their strength and their central limitation: the computation for position) Tj
T*
(t cannot begin until position t-1 has finished. Memory constraints then limit) Tj
T*
(batching across examples, and long sequences become expensive to train.) Tj
T*
() Tj
